      "source_number": "278",
      "independent_solution": "Use x_r = x_1*q^(r-1), obtained by r-1 successive multiplications by q. a) x_5 = x_1*q^4. b) x_21 = x_1*q^20. c) x_150 = x_1*q^149. d) x_m = x_1*q^(m-1). e) x_(m+2) = x_1*q^(m+1), since (m+2)-1 = m+1. f) x_(2k+1) = x_1*q^(2k), since (2k+1)-1 = 2k. Each named subscript must be a valid sequence index; the recurrence, rather than a convention about 0^0, gives the first term itself.",
      "mathematical_distinctions": [
        "All six requested terms are separate obligations, including the general and composite subscripts.",
        "The exponent is the term index minus one, not the index itself.",
        "No positivity assumption on q is supplied."
      ],
      "source_blockers": []
