      "source_number": "279",
      "independent_solution": "u_n = 256*(1/2)^(n-1) = 2^(9-n), for positive integer n. a) u_3 = 256/2^2 = 64. b) u_5 = 256/2^4 = 16. c) u_10 = 256/2^9 = 1/2. d) The requested general term is 256*(1/2)^(n-1), equivalently 2^(9-n). Substitution of n=1 recovers 256.",
      "mathematical_distinctions": [
        "The three numerical terms do not replace the fourth, symbolic general-term task.",
        "Halving occurs n-1 times; the tenth term is fractional, not 1."
      ],
      "source_blockers": []
