      "independent_solution": "Apply b_n = b_1*q^(n-1) separately to the four data sets. a) b_7 = 96*(1/2)^6 = 96/64 = 3/2. b) b_6 = 0.125*(-2)^5 = (1/8)*(-32) = -4. c) b_9 = 4*sqrt(2)*(-1/sqrt(2))^8 = 4*sqrt(2)/16 = sqrt(2)/4. d) b_7 = 0.003*(sqrt(10))^6 = 0.003*10^3 = 3.",
      "mathematical_distinctions": [
        "The negative ratios in b and c have odd and even exponents respectively, giving opposite sign outcomes.",
        "Radical powers in c and d must be evaluated before multiplying the initial term.",
        "All four sets are independent computations."
