      "source_number": "281",
      "independent_solution": "For a recurrence b_(n+1) = q*b_n, induction gives b_n = b_1*q^(n-1): it matches b_1, and multiplication by q yields the next exponent. a) b_n = 3*2^(n-1). b) b_n = 4*(-3)^(n-1). c) b_n = 25*5^(n-1) = 5^(n+1). d) b_n = 12*(1/2)^(n-1). In every case n is a positive integer and substitution at n=1 gives the stated initial term.",
      "mathematical_distinctions": [
